   <div class="note">
     <p>SRD items are from System Reference Document 5.2.1 by Wizards of the Coast LLC, licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0</a>. Retia items are from Lyre’s Guide to Retia: Land of Industry (pp. 516–518), summarised here. Retia’s firearms are listed together and are not split into simple or martial, so check the book. Ask your DM before using anything homebrew.</p>
+    <p><b>Kolvethis trick weapons</b> are homebrew for the Kor setting, built on Arsenal Row at Proof College. They are mundane, with no attunement, and each has two forms that copy the damage and properties of an official weapon (or a shield bash). A trick weapon has no Weapon Mastery. Once on each of your turns you can swap forms with no action, if you have the hands free for the new form. The first hit you land with the weapon on the turn you swapped triggers its Swap Strike, once per swap. A Swap Strike can name the form it fires on; if it names none, either swap triggers it. One that helps an ally can be delivered by touching a willing creature within reach, with no attack roll. One that calls for a saving throw takes the place of the attack roll. One marked “On swap” happens at the swap, with no hit needed. The save DC is 8 + your proficiency bonus + the ability modifier you attack with, and a condition from a save ends by the end of the target’s next turn. If a weapon needs a resource you don’t have, the swap still changes its form but there is no Swap Strike. Each House’s weapons share a build axis.</p>
